    "title": "Upholding Public Order: Sangguniang Bayan Conducts Legislative Hearing",
    "author": "LGU Kawayan",
    "date": "May 8, 2026",
    "image": "/news/07.jpg",
    "body": "The Office of the Sangguniang Bayan, spearheaded by the Committee on Peace and Order and Public Safety, held a vital public hearing on May 7 at the Legislative Building’s Conference Hall. This legislative exercise was organized in direct response to the Department of the Interior and Local Government (DILG) Memorandum Circular No. 2026-029. The primary objective was to vet a series of proposed ordinances designed to standardize public conduct and enhance the overall safety framework of the Municipality of Kawayan.\n\nA major focus of the hearing centered on social discipline and the regulation of public behavior. Among the drafted measures are ordinances strictly prohibiting topless or half-naked acts in public spaces and the consumption of intoxicating beverages in non-designated areas. These proposals aim to foster a more respectful and orderly environment, ensuring that communal spaces remain family-friendly and conducive to civil social interaction.\n\nIn addition to conduct-based regulations, the committee addressed noise pollution and youth safety. The proposed legislation includes strict regulations on the use of videoke machines and amplified audio devices, which have been a recurring concern for residential peace. Furthermore, the council deliberated on the institution of curfew hours for minors, specifically from 10:00 PM to 4:00 AM. This measure is intended to protect the youth from potential nocturnal hazards and encourage a more structured routine for students and children.\n\nThe hearing was characterized by an inclusive and rigorous deliberation process, featuring active participation from members of the Sangguniang Bayan, uniformed personnel, and Barangay Captains. The presence of local law enforcement was crucial in evaluating the enforceability of these rules, while the barangay leaders provided feedback on how these changes might impact their specific neighborhoods. This collaborative spirit ensures that the ordinances are not only legally sound but also practical for community-wide implementation.\n\nBy facilitating this open dialogue, the local government of Kawayan reaffirms its commitment to transparency and proactive governance. These proposed measures represent a significant step toward the municipality’s long-term vision of a peaceful and secure environment. As the ordinances move toward final approval, the administration continues to uphold the mantra #SaKawayanKayaYan, signaling that through collective discipline and clear regulation, the community can achieve a higher standard of public safety."
