    "title": "Empowering New Drivers: Free Theoretical Driving Course in Kawayan",
    "author": "LGU Kawayan",
    "date": "May 5, 2026",
    "image": "/news/11.jpg",
    "body": "The Municipality of Kawayan, in a strategic partnership with the Land Transportation Office (LTO) – Naval District, is proud to announce a FREE Theoretical Driving Course (TDC) scheduled for May 21–22, 2026. This two-day intensive program is designed to provide aspiring drivers with the foundational knowledge necessary to navigate the roads safely and legally. By offering this course at no cost, the local government aims to remove financial barriers for residents seeking to obtain their student permits and eventual driver’s licenses.\n\nThe sessions will run from 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM at the Function Hall of the Kawayan Municipal Building. Throughout the course, expert instructors from the LTO will cover essential topics, including road signs and markings, right-of-way rules, and the fundamental laws governing Philippine transportation. This comprehensive curriculum ensures that participants are not just memorizing answers for an exam, but are truly understanding the responsibilities that come with being behind the wheel.\n\nFor those eager to participate, the registration process has been made highly accessible. Interested individuals can secure their slot by scanning the provided QR code or accessing the official Google Forms link. Early registration is strongly encouraged, as slots are limited and the demand for formal driving education continues to grow. Applicants are also reminded to prepare all necessary identification and supporting documents as required by the LTO to ensure a smooth processing of their certificates upon completion of the course.\n\nThis initiative is a cornerstone of the municipality’s commitment to public safety and order. By educating the youth and new drivers on the principles of defensive driving and traffic discipline, the local government hopes to significantly reduce road accidents and promote a culture of mutual respect among motorists. It serves as a vital first step for citizens to transition from pedestrians to responsible, licensed operators who contribute to a more organized flow of traffic within the province.\n\nDon’t miss this chance to learn from the experts, comply with national licensing standards, and gain the confidence needed to hit the road. This program is a testament to the ongoing slogan #SaKawayanKayaYan, proving that through community cooperation and government support, professional growth and safety are within everyone's reach. Mark your calendars and take the lead in becoming a disciplined driver for a better, safer Kawayan."
