    "image": "/news/36.jpg",
    "body": "The Local Government Unit of Kawayan formally commenced its work week with a regular Flag Raising Ceremony on April 6, 2026, held at the Municipal Grounds. This weekly tradition serves as a vital cornerstone for the municipality, reinforcing the values of patriotism and professional integrity among public servants. By gathering the collective workforce before the start of official duties, the LGU maintains a disciplined environment focused on the shared goal of providing excellent public service to the Kawayanon people.\n\nThe ceremony saw a strong showing of municipal leadership, led by Vice Mayor Jake Espina along with the esteemed members of the Sangguniang Bayan. Also in attendance were various department heads, uniformed personnel, and the dedicated employees of the LGU. The presence of these officials underscores the importance of solidarity within the local government, ensuring that all branches of the administration—from legislative to executive and security—are aligned in their weekly objectives and operational standards.\n\nA significant highlight of the morning was the closing message delivered by Vice Mayor Espina, which took on a particularly meaningful tone given the timing of the event. With the observance of Holy Week approaching, the Vice Mayor spoke to the assembly about the profound significance of the season. He encouraged the staff to utilize the upcoming period as an essential time for rest and deep reflection, urging everyone to take a moment to step back from the rigors of office work and prioritize \"what truly matters\" in life and spirit.\n\nBeyond personal reflection, the Vice Mayor’s address served as a motivational call to action for the municipal workforce. He challenged all personnel to return from the Lenten break with a renewed sense of faith and a clarified purpose, which he noted are essential components for effective governance. By fostering a positive outlook and a heart for service, the Vice Mayor aims to cultivate an organizational culture where employees perform their duties not just as a requirement, but as a meaningful contribution to the town's progress.\n\nThe ceremony concluded on a high note of optimism, echoing the town's resilient spirit encapsulated in the hashtag #SaKawayanKayaYan. As the employees dispersed to their respective offices, the message of the morning remained a guiding theme: that a well-rested and spiritually grounded workforce is better equipped to handle the challenges of public administration. This regular assembly continues to be more than just a formality; it is a weekly realignment of the municipality’s commitment to service, faith, and community development."
